Z||000000||MrPBody||10-27-2000||11:46 PM||||Has anyone used IRM's high-durometer suspension bushings?  In principle, they look like a compromise between stock and polyurethane.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Wade87GT||10-28-2000||07:08 PM||||Hello MrPbody,<P>I haven't tried them on my Fiero but I have on my Triumph TR-8 (V8 version of the TR-7 conv.). I love them, they have the tightness of polys for more precise handing but they give a little when you hit larger bumps and potholes. Just what you need for a street car. Also, they don't have the "squeaks" you can get with the poly bushings. By the way, love the name you're using. I was going to start a Fiero shop using the name Peabody's (including the dog from Bullwinkle in the ad) but couldn't get copyright permission from Bill Ward (the Artist) to use his toon.||||reg||14
Z||000002||MrPBody||10-28-2000||08:54 PM||||TR8?  Now there's a rare one.  In a former life I worked on a few TR7's and Stags, but I think I never saw a TR8 in the flesh.  Did they use the Stag V8?<P>Who supplied TR8 bushings?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||rnoswal||10-29-2000||01:13 AM||||Yes!<P>Russ||||reg||1
Z||000004||MrPBody||10-29-2000||09:58 AM||||Does that mean: Yes, you used them and yes you like them?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Wade87GT||10-30-2000||10:23 AM||||MrPBody,<P>The TR-8s use the Rover aluminum 3.5L (215 c.i.) engine. It's the same engine used in the Range Rovers. It's also a direct desendent of the engine from the 61-63 Buick Special and the Olds Jetfire (turbocharged). The Stag used a Triumph designed V-8, which is so different that I don't think they even share any nuts and bolts. I bought my bushings (over ten years ago) from either Mountjoys or T.S. Imported Auto. They both specialize in 7s and 8s for street and racing. ||||reg||7
Z||000006||MrPBody||10-30-2000||05:00 PM||||Wade87GT --<P>Thanks for info (and a memory refresher).  I guess those sources don't stock Fiero bushings.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
